 "metres": {
  "how": "From the camera of data/scen.json. One camera gives no depth, so a wrist's speed and path are counted two ways. at_most: the wrist laid on a level plane 0.05 m over the felt, which makes a lift of the hand look like a long way in depth. at_least: the picture's steps taken as steps across the line of sight, which does not see a move toward or away from the camera. best: the geometric mean of the two. Tried on our own figure's films, where the truth is known (verktyg/docka.py): at_most came out 1.2 to 2.1 times the true top speed, at_least 0.6 to 0.7 times, and best within about a third of it; the same for the paths. So read best as true within a third, and the shapes and the seconds as well measured. The shoulders and the head are laid on an upright plane 0.2 m behind the dealer's edge of the felt; they move sideways and hold within about a tenth.",
  "camera_check_m": 0.0003,
  "shoulder_width_m": 0.357,
  "metres_per_pixel_at_the_shoulders": 0.00135
 },
