 "handover": {
  "how": "The hands are measured, not the card: the card is taken to be with the left hand until the two hands' grips are nearest each other, and with the right hand from then on. top_before is the left wrist's top speed on the way in, top_after the right wrist's on the way out, dip the lowest speed of the hand that has the card between those two tops (as metres a second, the best estimate of metres.how, and as a share of the higher top: 0 is a full stop, 1 no dip). curve is that speed from the one top to the other in 21 steps. On our own figure's film this way of measuring found one near stop where the figure's own numbers have three, so a short dip can be missed. Counted only where the right hand does carry on (over 0.3 m/s) after the meeting. An estimate until the card's own track is laid beside it.",
